{
  "summary": "The experiment tested an image-only model using ResNet50 without RNA data or fusion, achieving lower validation accuracy (0.208) and F1 (0.172) compared to RNA-only baselines. This suggests image data alone may underperform RNA-based approaches, but the low performance could be influenced by encoder choices or lack of aggregation. Further experiments are needed to compare different image encoders or fusion strategies to assess modality impact more accurately."
}

